%[text] %[text:anchor:H_FBCCFAEB] ## Step response
%[text] The output generated from a step input is known as the step response.
%[text]  ![SystemBoxStep.png](text:image:8733)
%[text]  *Response of a system to a step input.*
%[text] The step response is plotted in the time domain. Think of the step response as the system's response to a sustained constant forcing. In the vehicle model, this would result from continuously running the motor (with the assumption that it produced a constant traction force output).
%[text] ![brightbulb.png](text:image:4b03) **Reflect.** Consider the simple vehicle motion model. The input function is the traction force $u(t) = F\_{traction}(t)${"altText":"u(t) = F\_{traction}(t)"}.
%[text]  ![simpleCar.png](text:image:58c6)
%[text] - Try drawing a plot of the step response of the position transfer function $G(s) = X(s)/F(s)${"altText":"G(s) = X(s)\/F(s)"} in the time domain.
%[text] - Try drawing a plot of the step response of the velocity transfer function $H(s) = V(s)/F(s)${"altText":"H(s) = V(s)\/F(s)"} in the time domain. \
%%
